  production ragfarm-vision system prompt and Dave's own 1:1 request, verbatim.

  PROVENANCE — read before treating this as a model capability demo.
  The model's raw reply is NOT this file. It ran its full 24,576-token budget dry inside
  an edge repetition loop: 24 vertices, then 312 edges for a source that has ~26, 116 of
  them pointing at one node, and no closing </mxfile>. This file is that reply with one
  mechanical rule applied — keep every cell up to the FIRST repeated source/target pair
  (edge index 27), discard everything after it, close the document. Nothing was added,
  relabelled, repositioned or recoloured. The raw reply is in
  docs/measurements/2026-08-09-instruct-vs-thinking-drawio.json.

  FIDELITY against the PNG: 24 of 28 entities, correct labels, correct three-column
  layout, colours by domain. Missing: the per-entity attribute rows, the Legenda group,
  the PoC container frame, and the ER endpoint markers. It is a faithful skeleton, not
  the 1:1 copy that was asked for.
-->
